 "standard_text": "Understand and use the binomial expansion of (a + bx)ⁿ for positive integer n; the notations n! and ⁿCᵣ; link to binomial probabilities.",
 "meta_desc": "Free Year 12 A level maths worksheets on the binomial expansion: Pascal's triangle, nCr, coefficients of terms and expanding (a + bx)ⁿ. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "The term in xʳ of (a + bx)ⁿ is ⁿCᵣ aⁿ⁻ʳ (bx)ʳ.",
 "key_sub": "Remember to raise the number with x to the power too.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How it works</h2><p>(<i>a</i> + <i>b</i>)<sup>n</sup> = Σ ⁿC<sub>r</sub> <i>a</i><sup>n−r</sup><i>b</i><sup>r</sup>, where ⁿC<sub>r</sub> = <i>n</i>! ÷ (<i>r</i>!(<i>n</i> − <i>r</i>)!). The coefficients come from Pascal's triangle.</p><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Coefficient of <i>x</i>² in (1 + 3<i>x</i>)⁵.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>⁵C₂ × 3² = 10 × 9</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 90</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><ul><li>Writing 3x² instead of (3x)² = 9x².</li><li>Forgetting the sign when b is negative.</li><li>Using ⁿCᵣ with the wrong r.</li></ul>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "How do you find one term of a binomial expansion?",
   "a": "The term in xʳ of (a + bx)ⁿ is ⁿCᵣ × aⁿ⁻ʳ × (bx)ʳ. Work out the number part carefully."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is the sum of the coefficients?",
   "a": "Put x = 1. For (x + 3)⁴ the coefficients add up to 4⁴ = 256."
  }
 ],
